PROJECT: Cognitron AI — a goal-aware, personalized AI study companion for CBSE students.

STACK: React (frontend), Node.js/Express (backend), SQLite (database), LLM calls via 
[Anthropic/OpenAI — confirm which] API. Never train a custom model — all AI capability 
comes from calling an existing LLM's API.

CORE DATA MODEL:
- Student: { id, name, class, goal (class_test | midsem | board | competitive), subjects[] }
- Topic: { id, subject, chapter, name, prerequisites: [topic_id], mastery: 0-100 }
- StudySession: { student_id, topic_id, level (scratch | moderate | revision), time_budget_minutes }

DESIGN LANGUAGE:
Brand name: Cognitron AI (small sparkle/diamond mark next to the name)
Palette: soft lavender-purple primary (#7C6FE0 range), warm cream background (#F5F0E8), 
white cards with soft shadows, muted dark-charcoal text (#2E2A3D)
Typography: elegant serif for headings/decorative quotes (e.g. Playfair Display), 
clean sans-serif for body/nav text (e.g. Inter or Poppins)
Layout: left sidebar nav (Home, Learn, Practice, Test, Knowledge Map, AI Copilot/Doubt Box), 
top bar with search, date, notification bell, profile avatar
Cards: rounded corners (~18px radius), soft drop shadows, generous whitespace
Buttons: solid purple, pill-shaped, white text, right-arrow icon on primary CTAs
Progress display: LeetCode-style bubble cluster (one circle per topic, sized/colored by 
mastery), NOT a single aggregate ring

RULES:
- Keep components small and single-purpose
- Every feature must work against the CORE DATA MODEL above — don't invent a new shape per feature
- Comment any LLM prompt-construction code clearly, since teammates need to tweak wording
- Favor plain, readable code over cleverness — team needs to debug this live during the hackathon
- Never hardcode API keys — always read from environment variables